w: As | I was a-walk-ing one | morn-ing for pleas-ure, I | spied a cow-punch-er a- | rid-ing a-lone; His | hat was throwed back and his | spurs was a-jin-gling, And | as he ap-proached he was | sing-ing this song: Whoop-ee | ti-yi-yo, git a- | long, lit-tle do-gies, It's | your mis-for-tune and | none of my own: Whoop-ee | ti-yi-yo, git a- | long lit-tle do-gies, You | know that Wy-o-ming will | be your new home.
